Here is another version of usleep that should work on all bsdish systems
(and maybe on sys5 as well) -- (we didn't have usleep here)

void usleep(long val)
{
  struct timeval tout;

  tout.tv_sec = 0;
  tout.tv_usec = val;
  (void)select(32, 0, 0, 0, &tout);
}

(this might require you putting a #include <time.h> at the top.. it didn't
for my system)

